WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:08.050
Before him, chemists drew compounds as a clutter of little pictograms circles,

2
00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:09.950
crescents, fragments of alchemy.

3
00:00:10.733 --> 00:00:15.453
Berzelius proposed something almost insultingly simple: "The chemical signs ought to

4
00:00:15.453 --> 00:00:20.133
be letters... I shall take, therefore, for the chemical sign, the initial letter of

5
00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:25.413
the Latin name." Every time you write Fe for iron or balance an equation, you are

6
00:00:25.413 --> 00:00:27.333
using the grammar he laid on the page.

7
00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:32.413
He ran his empire of measurement out of a converted kitchen in Stockholm, heating

8
00:00:32.413 --> 00:00:37.213
samples on a domestic sand bath, and from that kitchen he measured the atomic

9
00:00:37.213 --> 00:00:41.753
weights of 45 elements to within a few percent of the values we use today.

10
00:00:42.313 --> 00:00:46.673
He also coined protein and catalysis, two words this course cannot do without.

11
00:00:47.483 --> 00:00:48.963
And he was exacting.

12
00:00:49.583 --> 00:00:54.463
When the young Friedrich Wöhler rushed his first analysis in that kitchen, Berzelius

13
00:00:54.463 --> 00:00:59.663
glanced at it and handed down a verdict that trailed Wöhler for life: "Doctor, that

14
00:00:59.663 --> 00:01:01.083
was quickly and badly done."

15
00:01:01.783 --> 00:01:04.403
The sample was swept aside, to be done again.

16
00:01:05.123 --> 00:01:09.463
Speed without care counted for nothing the standard this whole field is built on.
